Do what makes you feel alive. And build a life where you don’t have to escape your everyday existence to feel that way.

Chase wonder. Create things. Love fiercely. Play. Explore. Take chances worth taking. Laugh until it hurts.

And remember that feeling alive doesn’t always require adrenaline, danger, or intensity.

Sometimes it’s adventure. Sometimes it’s peace. Sometimes it’s watching your children discover something you’ve forgotten was magical.

Don’t confuse being alive with merely surviving. And don’t confuse being at peace with standing still.

You can choose to enjoy the ride, even while you’re building the road.

It’s your life, my friend. Live it. ;)